Snappy 1.3.1 remains the pkgsrc common package and uses the upstream Apache-2.0
license and archive hashes. EmberBSD adds a package-owned pkg-config file so
native and cross consumers can select the same installed library and headers;
the metadata change does not alter the library or its ABI.
Native Darwin arm64 and cross NetBSD amd64 package-only metadata repackaging
passed the normal staged PLIST and package checks. Both nb1 package manifests
list snappy.pc with its matching MD5 and identify devel/snappy in +BUILD_INFO.
No package was installed and target execution was not tested.
